On Feb 26, 2012, at 4:07 PM, rkkalathur at ualg.pt wrote:

> Dear Simon,
> We are using Rserve to perform computations for enrichment analysis in R and using bioconductor. Our server is linux. We are trying to dispaly the results on the web after performing necessary actions on the server which is linux. While performing the computations first time we are getting the result, but at the next instance we get an error (Null point exception error).
> 

I cannot replicate it with the code you sent (well, the code is incomplete so I had to remove the FAE stuff and use StartRserve from Rserve itself). I ran it both on Ubuntu and OS X and it worked just fine.

You are shutting down the Rserve - is that intentional? Obviously, that will only allow you to run one request ... and it completely defeats the purpose of Rserve which is to avoid startup-delays. If you are more serious about your application, you should move all your initializations code into Rserve (just loading BioC packages takes forever so you really don't want to do that in your request).

That said, it is certainly possible to start Rserve, use it and shut it down, but you can't issue any additional request until a full shutdown, so chances that that's what you are trying (but not in the posted code). Note that c.shutdown() is really very crude, it is much safer and cleaner to use serverShutdown() -- in fact future version of Rserve will likely replace shutdown() with serverShutdown() internally.

Cheers,
Simon


